<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Nicopolis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1396</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Nicopolis was fought on 25 September 1396 at Nicopolis on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. A crusading army led by King Sigismund of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, with French, Burgundian and other Western knights, was routed by the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>. The defeat ended the last large-scale joint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> firmly in control of Bulgaria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-nicopolis.jpg" alt="Battle of Nicopolis" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sébastien Mamerot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NikopolisSchlacht.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
